      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 0,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "AB InBev is a multinational drink and brewing company headquartered in Leuven, Belgium. It is the world's largest brewer and operates over 500 beer brands, including Budweiser, Corona, and Stella Artois. The company prioritizes sustainability and is actively working towards reducing its carbon footprint and water usage.",
            "type": "text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": null,
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "paragraph",
        "version": 1,
        "textFormat": 0,
        "textStyle": ""
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 0,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "AB InBev operates on a business model that centers around producing, distributing, and selling a diverse range of alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages. The scale of their operations allows them to have a significant presence in the global market, and they are continuously innovating their portfolio through acquisitions and brand development. Recent developments include a stronger focus on digital transformation and e-commerce platforms to align with changing consumer preferences.",
            "type": "text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": null,
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "paragraph",
